ent B: The survey was conducted in at least three schools.**\n     - This statement is true. Since the survey results were consistent across all three schools, it is clear that at least three schools were involved in the survey. This statement is supported by the given information.\n   \n   - **Statement C: The survey was conducted in more than three schools.**\n     - This statement is not necessarily true. The survey could have been conducted in exactly three schools, as long as the distribution of preferences was consistent across all three schools. Therefore, this statement is not guaranteed to be true.\n   \n   - **Statement D: The survey was conducted in at most three schools.**\n     - This statement is not necessarily true. The survey could have been conducted in more than three schools, as long as the distribution of preferences was consistent across all schools. Therefore, this statement is not guaranteed to be true.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Based on the information provided, the statement that must be true is:\n     B) The survey was conducted in at least three schools.\n\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
