s a general tendency to doubt decisions and be resistant to restrictions. It does not involve a vague personality description that people believe applies to them.\n   - This does not fit the Barnum effect.\nBased on the analysis, the correct option that exemplifies the Barnum effect is Option C.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC\n</answer>",
