ldren because the listening to books in parent-child reading is not counted.\n- This option provides a plausible explanation for why the number of books read by children decreased despite increased reading habits among parents.\n- This option directly addresses the observed phenomenon.\n\nD) Electronic reading by parents on mobile phones and computers has not been taken into account in children's books.\n- This option suggests that electronic reading by parents might not be included in the count of books read by children. However, it does not directly explain why the number of books read by children decreased.\n- This option does not provide a clear explanation for the observed phenomenon.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the one that best explains the phenomenon is option C.\n</answer>",
